		{"id":"7d331877754856d5","type":"text","text":"This table compares your project’s idea for automated Text-to-SQL scaling with the four research papers provided in the sources.\n\n| Paper / Project                      | Year  | Main Goal                                                                                                 | Methodology & Technology                                                                           | Validation / Scoring Strategy                                                                                                         | Comparison                                                                                                        | Gaps (4 Points)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | Potential Exploration                                                                             |\n| :----------------------------------- | :---- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Your Project (NL2SQL Scaling)**    | 2024* | Scale Text-to-SQL datasets from small seeds to many variations without human labeling.                    | LLaMA 3.1, Mistral, Qwen, and **vLLM engine** for a two-stage NL2NL and NL2SQL pipeline.           | **Solvability Set (S(Q)):** Paraphrases are accepted if models that solved the original also solve the variation via execution match. | **Baseline Reference.**                                                                                           | 1. Relies on **\"lucky\" execution matches** where wrong SQL yields correct results. <br> 2. Vulnerable to **shared model biases** within the Solvability Set. <br> 3. **Linguistic flavor** limited by LLaMA-only paraphrasing. <br> 4. No current evaluation of **SQL execution efficiency**.   | Better diversity metrics, multi-model paraphrase ensembles, and improved verification thresholds. |\n| **Enhancing BERT Sensitivity**       | 2024  | Enhance BERT robustness against variations in question phrasing and distracting document details.         | BERT Large, data augmentation via **back-translation** (Mandarin/Dutch), and multitask learning.   | **Unsupervised Loss:** Minimizes **KL divergence** or JS distance between original and augmented answer distributions.                | Uses **distribution-based** internal AI validation vs. your project's **execution-based** result validation.      | 1. **Diversity limits** in the chosen back-translation approach. <br> 2. High risk of **overfitting** to new language structures. <br> 3. Focused on **outdated architectures** (BERT) compared to modern LLMs. <br> 4. Difficulty maintaining **semantic equivalence** across pivot languages. | Using weight annealing for auxiliary loss and more sophisticated paraphrase generation.           |\n| **Learning to Paraphrase (PARA4QA)** | 2017  | Framework to learn and **weight paraphrases** most likely to yield correct answers for various QA tasks.  | **Bi-LSTM** neural scoring model; generation via PPDB, NMT pivoting, and WikiAnswers rules.        | **Neural Weighting:** Assigns higher weights to candidates likely to produce correct answers via joint end-to-end training.           | Weighting paraphrases **during inference** to find an answer vs. your **offline scaling** of a dataset.           | 1. Scoring model is **independent** of the internal QA system state. <br> 2. **Candidate set size** is restricted to maintain tractability. <br> 3. Scoring features (POS tags, etc.) are often **uninformative**. <br> 4. Relies on **older Bi-LSTM** technology.                              | Advanced attention-based scoring models and exploring additional paraphrase generators.           |\n| **ParaQA (Dataset)**                 | 2021  | Create a dataset with **multiple paraphrased answer responses** for expressive single-turn conversation.  | Semi-automated framework; **NER** for entity-type ID, Gender identification, and back-translation. | **Human Peer-Review:** A manual rectification process ensures grammatical correctness and natural flow.                               | Paraphrases the **answers** for user flexibility vs. your focus on paraphrasing **questions** for model training. | 1. Limited to **single-turn** conversation only. <br> 2. **High human dependency** for final rectification. <br> 3. **Scalability costs** make manual peer-review expensive. <br> 4. Does not address **multi-turn context**.                                                                   | Supporting multi-turn conversations and combining them with paraphrased questions.                |\n| **Recovering QA Errors**             | 2016  | Provide a **post-inspection component** to recover from prediction errors by cross-checking KB relations. | **Bidirectional LSTM**; Entity-centric, Answer-centric, and Relation-centric \"query revisions\".    | **Consistency Scoring:** A hinge-loss objective checks if a revised question \"makes sense\" given a candidate relation.                | A **corrective tool** at the end of a pipeline vs. your project’s **scaling tool** for data generation.           | 1. Evaluation restricted to **1-hop and 2-hop** relations only. <br> 2. Heavily dependent on the **external base system's** initial ranking. <br> 3. Success is tied to **NER tagger accuracy** for entity spans. <br> 4. Lacks ability to reason over **raw text** evidence.                   | Accommodating text evidence directly without the need for explicit question revision.             |\n\n*\\*Year inferred from contemporary technology use (LLaMA 3.1) and project context.*","x":-2391,"y":471,"width":2222,"height":1140},
